 |M|=2,3 fails)"})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-white/[0.02] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] text-white/30",children:"WHY 4?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-sans text-[12px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"2 fails closure, 3 fails equilibrium (odd). 4 is first even closure. Not assumed — derived."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-white/[0.02] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] text-white/30",children:"GEOMETRY"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-sans text-[12px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Four vectors in R³ at equal mutual angle → tetrahedron. Gram matrix Gᵢⱼ = vᵢ·vⱼ."})]})]})]}),s("div",{className:"space-y-4",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[14px] border border-[#00f0ff]/20 bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.04] p-5",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"GRAM MATRIX — L1 OUTPUT"}),s("div",{className:"mt-3 font-mono text-[12px] leading-[1.8] text-white/80",children:[u("div",{children:"G = [[1, c, c, c],"}),u("div",{className:"pl-6",children:"[c, 1, c, c],"}),u("div",{className:"pl-6",children:"[c, c, 1, c],"}),u("div",{className:"pl-6",children:"[c, c, c, 1]]"}),u("div",{className:"mt-2 text-white/40",children:"where c = vᵢ·vⱼ for i≠j, |vᵢ|=1"})]})]}),u(ti,{title:"ELIMINATION: |M|=2",text:"Two magnitudes cannot close under composition without identity collapse. Violates equilibrium (Σ=0 requires at least 3 signed terms).",accent:"red"}),u(ti,{title:"ELIMINATION: |M|=3",text:"Three magnitudes yield odd closure cycle. Determinant of Gram never zero for equilibrium in R³ — requires embedding in R⁴, breaking territory-first (R³) premise.",accent:"gold"})]})]})]}),s("div",{className:"md:col-span-12 mt-10",children:[u(On,{num:"L2",title:"Invariant c = −1/3 Forced by Equilibrium",mono:"L2 — NO FREE PARAMETER"}),u("div",{className:"mt-4