ver"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-2 font-sans text-[12px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Angle between any two distinct fragment vectors: arccos(−1/3) ≈ 109.47° — tetrahedral angle. Not chosen for beauty. Forced by det=0 in R³."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[12px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-white/[0.02] p-5",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] text-white/40",children:"WHY NOT c=1?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-2 font-sans text-[12px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"c=1 gives G = J (all ones) → rank 1 → all vectors identical. Magnitude equilibrium would be identity, not relation. Eliminated by non-degeneracy: fragment must span R³."})]})]})]})})]}),s("div",{className:"md:col-span-12 mt-10",children:[u(On,{num:"L3",title:"Trace vs Territory — The 4D Mirror",mono:"EPISTEMOLOGY — OPTICAL TRACE IS ONE TRACE AMONG MANY"}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[14px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0f0f18] p-6",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/40",children:"FORMAL DISTINCTION"}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 space-y-4 font-mono text-[12px] leading-[1.7]",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] bg-white/[0.03] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"text-white/50",children:"TERRITORY R³"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 text-white/80",children:"Real 3D structure: fragment vectors at c=−1/3, screw rotations, period domains. Exists independent of observer."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"text-[#00f0ff]",children:"TRACE T²"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 text-white/70",children:"2D projection via sensor P: optical P_opt, acoustic P_ac, haptic P_hap, etc. Each P is lossy."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] bg-[#ffd700]/[0.08] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"text-[#ffd700]",children:"MIRROR M⁴ = I(T²)"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 text-white/70",children:"Brain/LLM builds 4D inference from trace 