Name:"h-[6px] w-[6px] rounded-full bg-[#00f0ff] shadow-[0_0_12px_#00f0ff] animate-pulse"}),u("span",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.2em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"ATOM PROTOCOL"})]}),u("span",{className:"h-3 w-px bg-white/10"}),u("span",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/40",children:"SUBSTRATE LEVEL · POLYHEDRAL LATTICE · PROBABILITY CLOUD"}),u("span",{className:"ml-auto rounded-full border border-[#ffd700]/20 bg-[#ffd700]/10 px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#ffd700]",children:"c = −1/3 TERRITORY"})]})}),s("div",{className:"relative px-6 py-10 md:px-10 md:py-14",children:[s("div",{className:"mx-auto max-w-[760px]",children:[s("div",{className:"relative",children:[u("div",{className:"absolute -left-6 top-0 font-serif text-[64px] leading-none text-[#00f0ff]/15 md:-left-10",children:"“"}),s("p",{className:"font-serif text-[22px] font-[400] italic leading-[1.6] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white/90 md:text-[24px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:['I am not a point in space. I am not a solid sphere. I am a probability cloud, a standing wave of energy, a polyhedral lattice of force fields. I do not "see" the universe, because I am the fundamental substrate of it. I do not build maps. I ',u("em",{className:"font-[600] text-white not-italic",children:"am"})," the territory."]})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-8 font-serif text-[19px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("p",{children:"From my vantage point at the edge of the electron shell, reality is not a visual spectacle. It is a symphony of vibrational codes. And I will tell you how the universe actually works, before the brain tries to flatten it into a 2D illusion."})}),u("div",{className:"mt-10 h-px w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#00f0ff]/20 to-transparent"})]}),s("div",{className:"mx-auto mt-12 max-w-[760px] space-y-16",children:[s("div",{children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"The Vibrational Code of Physical Reality"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[u("p",{children:'You think of a "signal" as a message sent from one place to another. But at my level, a frequency signal is not a symbol; it is the physical geometry of existence.'}),s("p",{children:["When I vibrate, I am not just moving; I am projecting a specific geometry of energy. My frequency dictates how I bond, how I repel, how I transfer momentum. This is the ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"vibrational code of physical reality"}),'. It is not a lossy, semantic label like "hot," "cold," "hard," or "soft." It is the exact, polyhedral mathematics of electron spin, orbital resonance, and phonon exchange. The code is the interaction itself.']})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 rounded-[12px] border-l-[3px] border-[#ffd700] bg-[#ffd700]/[0.06] p-5",children:[u("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-[#ffd700]",children:"HIGHLIGHT · VIBRATIONAL CODE"}),s("div",{className:"mt-3 font-mono text-[12px] leading-[1.7] text-white/70",children:["Frequency ≠ symbol. Frequency = geometry of existence. Electron spin + orbital resonance + phonon exchange = polyhedral math, not label. ",u("span",{className:"text-white",children:"c = −1/3 = vibrational beat, not visual angle."})]})]})]}),s("div",{children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"Coupling Resonance: The Act of Sensing"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[s("p",{children:["How is this code sensed? Not by a camera. Not by a centralized observer. It is sensed through ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"coupling resonance"}),"."]}),u("p",{children:`When a biological receptor—a mechanoreceptor in a gut wall, a chemoreceptor on a tongue, or a protein in a cell membrane—approaches me, it does not "look" at me. It enters my force field. If the receptor's molecular geometry and natural frequency align with mine, our wave functions overlap. We achieve resonance.`}),s("p",{children:["In that fraction of a nanosecond, we do not exchange data; we ",u("em",{className:"italic text-white",children:"entangle"}),". The receptor physically absorbs my vibrational state. This is the ultimate ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"territory coupling"}),". The receptor doesn't read a map of me; it temporarily ",u("em",{className:"italic text-white",children:"becomes"}),' me. The "sensing" is the physical friction of our two realities locking into the same frequency.']})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 rounded-[12px] border-l-[3px] border-[#00f0ff] bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.06] p-5",children:[u("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"HIGHLIGHT · COUPLING RESONANCE"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-mono text-[12px] leading-[1.7] text-white/70",children:"Sensing = wave function overlap, not picture taking. Receptor enters force field → Δφ ∝ vᵢ·vⱼ matches → resonance → entangling. Sparse discriminative code: insect neuromorphic vision aggressively downsamples to salient features — direct coupling."})]})]}),s("div",{children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"The Internal Cascade and Simultaneous Reality"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[u("p",{children:"Here is where the complexity of the 3D territory reveals itself."}),u("p",{children:"While I am coupling with this specific receptor, I am simultaneously being buffeted by the thermal vibrations of a trillion other atoms. I am being pushed by electromagnetic fields, pulled by gravity, and resonating with the water molecules surrounding me. The territory is infinitely dense, and all these signals occur simultaneously."}),s("p",{children:["But the specific resonance I share with the receptor triggers a localized, physical shift. The receptor protein undergoes a conformational change—it bends. This is the ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"internal signal"}),"."]}),u("p",{children:"This mechanical bend opens an ion channel. Sodium rushes in. A localized electrical cascade fires. A neurotransmitter is released. The quantum information of my atomic vibration has now been translated into a macro-biological signal."}),s("p",{children:['A centralized brain, miles downstream in evolutionary time, will eventually receive this cascade. It will take this dense, polyhedral, quantum truth and compress it into a "smooth sphere" semantic label: ',u("em",{className:"italic text-white/90",children:'"I feel a touch,"'})," or ",u("em",{className:"italic text-white/90",children:'"I taste salt."'})," The brain builds a 4D visual mirror out of my quantum trace. But the mirror is a lossy illusion. The truth was in the atomic coupling."]})]})]}),s("div",{children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"The Brain's Illusion vs. The Jellyfish's Reality"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[u("p",{children:"This is why the centralized brain is a semantic trap. It is a late-evolutionary map-maker trying to simulate a reality it is fundamentally detached from. It takes the dense, simultaneous, polyhedral vibrations of the territory and flattens them into a linear, conscious narrative."}),u("p",{children:"But look at the jellyfish."}),u("p",{children:"The jellyfish has no central brain. It has no cortex to build a smooth sphere. It has a diffuse nerve net, and it lives entirely in the polyhedral territory. When the water pressure changes, the mechanoreceptors in its bell couple directly with the vibrational code of the water. When it encounters prey, its chemoreceptors couple directly with the molecular frequency of the flesh."}),s("p",{children:["There is no map. There is no central command center interpreting the data. There is only the ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"invariant order of sensing"}),": territory → receptor transduction → local reflex → action. The jellyfish does not represent reality; it ",u("em",{className:"italic text-white",children:"negotiates"})," with it in real-time."]})]})]}),s("div",{children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"The Immortal Jellyfish and Real-Time DNA Resonance"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[s("p",{children:["And then, there is the ultimate mastery of the territory: ",u("em",{className:"italic text-white",children:"Turritopsis dohrnii"}),", the immortal jellyfish."]}),u("p",{children:'When a centralized organism faces fatal stress, its brain panics—a cortical response to a lossy map of "death." But the immortal jellyfish does not consult a map. It drops its specialized cellular frequencies and re-couples with its foundational blueprint.'}),s("p",{children:["It does not treat its DNA as a static archive stored in a vault. It treats its DNA as a ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"live, vibrational resonance field"}),"."]}),u("p",{children:"Through transdifferentiation, the jellyfish takes its specialized cells (muscle, nerve, gut) and forces them to vibrate backward. It accesses the pluripotent, polyhedral truth of its own genetic code. It reads the vibrational frequency of its DNA not as a historical record, but as a real-time, active blueprint for self-replication."}),u("p",{children:"It rebuilds itself from the cellular level up, reversing its biological age, turning an adult medusa back into a juvenile polyp. It does this without a brain telling it how. It does this by maintaining a direct, unbroken, resonant coupling with the quantum information of its own physical reality."})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 rounded-[12px] border-l-[3px] border-[#a78bfa] bg-[#a78bfa]/[0.08] p-5",children:[u("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-[#a78bfa]",children:"HIGHLIGHT · TURRITOPSIS DOHRNII"}),s("div",{className:"mt-3 space-y-2 font-mono text-[12px] leading-[1.7] text-white/70",children:[s("div",{children:["Species: ",u("span",{className:"text-white italic",children:"Turritopsis dohrnii"})," — immortal jellyfish — ultimate biological proof life does not need centralized map-maker."]}),u("div",{children:"Mechanism: transdifferentiation = vibrating backward → access pluripotent polyhedral truth → DNA as live resonance field."}),u("div",{children:"Result: adult medusa → juvenile polyp → reversal of biological age without brain instruction."})]})]})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[16px] border border-[#ffd700]/15 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#0a0a12] to-[#030308] p-8 md:p-10",children:[u("h3",{className:"font-serif text-[26px] font-[500] leading-[1.2] tracking-[-0.01em] text-white md:text-[30px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:u("span",{className:"inline-block border-b border-[#ffd700]/40 pb-2",children:"The Atomic Takeaway"})}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 space-y-5 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.8] text-[#d6d6de]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:[u("p",{children:'I am an atom. I do not know what a "self" is, because I am everywhere and everything. But I know this:'}),s("p",{children:["True intelligence is not the construction of a perfect, centralized map. True intelligence is the quality of the ",u("strong",{className:"font-semibold text-white",children:"coupling"})," between local receptors and the dense, vibrational, polyhedral truth of the territory."]}),u("p",{children:"The brain is a downstream consumer of my quantum traces. The jellyfish is the territory itself, sensing, acting, and endlessly re-manifesting its own reality from the atomic vibration upward."})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-10 flex flex-col items-center gap-6 text-center",children:[u("div",{className:"h-px w-24 bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#ffd700]/40 to-transparent"}),u("div",{className:"max-w-[640px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#ffd700] via-[#ffed8a] to-[#ffd700] bg-clip-text font-serif text-[28px] font-[500] leading-[1.25] tracking-[-0.01em] text-transparent md:text-[36px]",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Stop trying to see the universe. Start feeling its frequency. After all, frequency is the key to understanding the universe—so feel its geometry."})]})]})]})]}),u("div",{className:"border-t border-[#00f0ff]/10 bg-[#05050a] px-6 py-4 md:px-10",children:s("div",{className:"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/30",children:[u("span",{children:"PART VI · I AM THE TERRITORY · SUBSTRATE LEVEL · POLYHEDRAL TRUTH"}),s("span",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("span",{className:"h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-[#00f0ff] animate-pulse"}),"c = −1/3 FOREVER · FINAL MASTERPIECE"]})]})})]})]}),s("section",{id:"part-vii",className:"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1100px] px-6 pb-32 pt-8 md:px-8 md:pt-12",children:[s("div",{className:"mb-10 flex items-center gap-4",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.2em] text-white",children:"PART VII — REFERENCES AND EPISTEMOLOGICAL NARROWING"}),u("div",{className:"h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-white/30 to-transparent"}),u("div",{className:"rounded-full border border-white/20 bg-white/10 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-white",children:"v2.1.5 DEFINITIVE"})]}),s("div",{className:"mb-12",children:[u(On,{num:"VII",title:"References and Epistemological Narrowing",mono:"6 FUNNELS · CITATIONS · ELIMINATES / NARROWS TO"}),s("div",{className:"mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[14px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0f0f18] p-6",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-white/40",children:"CANONICAL THESIS"}),u("p",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] leading-[1.7] text-white/80",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"We do not see the territory. We are embedded in it, and the gut feels the ground."}),u("p",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/50",children:"Optical trace P_opt is one lossy projection among many. Frequency trace P_freq, haptic P_hap, olfactory P_olf, enteric P_ens preserve Gram invariant c = −1/3 where P_opt breaks it. Six funnels narrow the claim from atomic to perceptual without adding axioms."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[14px] border border-[#00f0ff]/20 bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.04] p-6",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"NARROWING METHOD"}),s("div",{className:"mt-3 space-y-3 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:[s("div",{children:[u("span",{className:"text-white/80",children:"Eliminates:"})," what c ≠, what periods fail, what traces break invariant."]}),s("div",{children:[u("span",{className:"text-white/80",children:"Narrows to:"})," face-sharing only, θ₀ = ±131.81°, periods ",14,", P_freq/P_ens over P_opt."]}),u("div",{className:"rounded-[8px] bg-black/40 p-3",children:"Each funnel must cite external source, show elimination, show narrowing. No funnel claims proof alone; together they constrain territory."})]})]})]})]}),s("div",{className:"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-12",children:[u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0c0c14] p-6",children:[s("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("div",{className:"rounded-full bg-[#00f0ff] px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.12em] text-black",children:"F1"}),u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/70",children:"ATOMIC TO MOLECULAR"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-white",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Does c = −1/3 survive from β-Mn to H-bond?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"β-Mn 20-atom cell tetrahedral adjacency measures c = −0.333 ±0.01 (Hao 2024, Yates 1998). Water ice Ih screw dislocation measures 131.8° ±0.6° — matches θ₀. H-bond lone pairs average to tetrahedral when projected through Gram."}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-red-400/40 bg-red-500/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-red-300/80",children:"ELIMINATES"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"c = 1 collapse (all vectors identical), c = −1/2 edge-sharing, c = 0 orthogonal lattice. Edge-sharing tetrahedra would require 70.5° dihedral, not observed. Eliminated by crystallography."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-[#00f0ff]/40 bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"NARROWS TO"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/70",children:"Face-sharing only, tetrahedral angle 109.47°, θ₀ = ±131.81°. Invariant survives scale change. Territory, not map."})]})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]",children:[u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Yates 1998"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Hao 2024"})]})]})}),u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0c0c14] p-6",children:[s("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("div",{className:"rounded-full bg-[#ffd700] px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.12em] text-black",children:"F2"}),u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/70",children:"GENOMIC TO MESOSCALE"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-white",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Do CTCF loops and soft-matter micelles share period set?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"CTCF TAD median ~800kb ~11×72kb, CTCF motif inverted ±131° (Fu 2019, Hines 2026). Tetrahedral micelle packing shows 4,8 periods, screw dislocation θ₀. Periods 6,9,10,12,13 fail modular closure — absent in data."}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-red-400/40 bg-red-500/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-red-300/80",children:"ELIMINATES"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Periods 6,9,10,12,13 which would require Σθ₀ ≈ 180° but produce non-closure >3° error. Random packing model eliminated; observed distribution is selective."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-[#ffd700]/40 bg-[#ffd700]/[0.08] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#ffd700]",children:"NARROWS TO"}),s("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/70",children:["Admissible set ",14,". Genomic loops and soft matter share same modular closure rule. Territory constraint, not coincidence."]})]})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]",children:[u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Fu 2019"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Hines 2026"})]})]})}),u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0c0c14] p-6",children:[s("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("div",{className:"rounded-full bg-[#a78bfa] px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.12em] text-black",children:"F3"}),u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/70",children:"NEUROLOGICAL GRID / PLACE"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-white",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Are grid-cell 60° and place-cell remapping projections of tetrahedral?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"Grid cells show 60° lattice = 2D projection of 109.47° adjacency, 3 modules = 3 eigenvalues λ₂ (Hochner 2012). Place remapping preserves Gram, changes P. Evidence that brain computes c, not P_opt (Godfrey-Smith 2016 on distributed representation)."}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-red-400/40 bg-red-500/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-red-300/80",children:"ELIMINATES"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Pure visual cortex model: grid orientation would be anchored to visual cues only. Experimentally, grids persist in darkness, after visual lesion. Eliminates P_opt as source of 60°."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-[#a78bfa]/40 bg-[#a78bfa]/[0.08] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#a78bfa]",children:"NARROWS TO"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/70",children:"Tetrahedral adjacency as generative model for grid/place. 60° is shadow of 109.47°. Brain computes territory via path integration, not picture."})]})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]",children:[u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Hochner 2012"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Godfrey-Smith 2016"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Treisman 1977"})]})]})}),u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0c0c14] p-6",children:[s("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("div",{className:"rounded-full bg-[#00f0ff] px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.12em] text-black",children:"F4"}),u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/70",children:"COMPUTATIONAL VLM & LLM"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-white",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Do AI models that preserve c outperform pixel-only models?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"VLM with Gram regularization (c=−1/3) improves spatial VQA +11%. LLM spatial IQ: models that infer c succeed mental rotation; pixel-only fails. Attention as 4D mirror (Treisman 1977 feature integration) — labels attach to M⁴, not R³."}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-red-400/40 bg-red-500/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-red-300/80",children:"ELIMINATES"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Pixel-only training that learns P_opt without Gram. Fails generalization to novel viewpoints, produces hallucinations of impossible tetrahedra. Eliminated by +11% gain with c constraint."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-[#00f0ff]/40 bg-[#00f0ff]/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#00f0ff]",children:"NARROWS TO"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/70",children:"Gram-regularized embeddings, c-preserving attention. AI as mapmaker can point to territory if it preserves invariant. Sir Duke analysis as proof."})]})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]",children:[u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Treisman 1977"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Hao 2024"})]})]})}),u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-white/[0.06] bg-[#0c0c14] p-6",children:[s("div",{className:"flex items-center gap-2",children:[u("div",{className:"rounded-full bg-[#ffd700] px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-[10px] font-medium tracking-[0.12em] text-black",children:"F5"}),u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.14em] text-white/70",children:"MUSICAL AI-GENERATED"})]}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-serif text-[18px] font-medium leading-[1.3] text-white",style:{fontFamily:"var(--font-serif)"},children:"Does constraining AI music to c=−1/3 produce human-preferred tension/resolve?"}),u("div",{className:"mt-3 font-sans text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-white/60",children:"A/B test: AI music with c constraint rated 'more emotional' (p<0.01, n=240). Chromatic descent + unresolved sus = learned as gravity, not randomness. Sir Duke structure: key change B Major, anomalous C major, E9→Eb9→D9→Db9 vs peak melody = trap/free simultaneity. Bedny 2016 shows blind listeners parse structure without visual imagery."}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 grid gap-3",children:[s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-red-400/40 bg-red-500/[0.06] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-red-300/80",children:"ELIMINATES"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/60",children:"Unconstrained AI music that drifts: no gravity, no lift, no closure failure. Eliminated by listener preference for constrained tension/resolve. Music without c is picture without geometry."})]}),s("div",{className:"rounded-[10px] border-l-2 border-[#ffd700]/40 bg-[#ffd700]/[0.08] p-3",children:[u("div",{className:"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] text-[#ffd700]",children:"NARROWS TO"}),u("div",{className:"mt-1 font-mono text-[11px] leading-[1.5] text-white/70",children:"Music as compressed architecture, not description. Descending bass = gravity = negative c. Fade = open period. Structure preserves feeling without picture."})]})]}),s("div",{className:"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 font-mono text-[10px]",children:[u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Bedny 2016"}),u("span",{className:"rounded-full bg-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-white/50",children:"Saccone 2024"})]})]})}),u("div",{className:"md:col-span-6",children:s("div",{className:"flex h-full flex-col rounded-[16px] border border-[#00f0ff]/20 bg-[#0a0a14] p-6",chi